What is the output of the following fluent setter pattern program?
```java
class RequestOption {
    private int timeout = 1000;
    public RequestOption setTimeout(int ms) {
        if (ms > 0) this.timeout = ms;
        return this;
    }
    public int getTimeout() {
        return timeout;
    }
}
public class FluentApp {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        RequestOption opt = new RequestOption().setTimeout(5000);
        System.out.println(opt.getTimeout());
    }
}
```

What happens when an exception is thrown inside a validating setter?
```java
class VolumeControl {
    private int level = 5;
    public void setLevel(int l) {
        if (l < 0 || l > 10) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Out of bounds");
        }
        this.level = l;
    }
    public int getLevel() { return level; }
}
public class VolumeApp {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        VolumeControl vc = new VolumeControl();
        try {
            vc.setLevel(15);
        } catch (IllegalArgumentException e) {}
        System.out.println(vc.getLevel());
    }
}
```

